A||N||4||dennis_6||86 SE engine problems||||1||
Z||000000||dennis_6||08-22-2001||02:29 AM||||I have an 86 Fiero SE with a 2.8l v6 and a auto tranny.  When started the fiero idles high up to 3k RPM and slowly bleeds off the rpms and then dies unless you floor the gas pedal.  If you floor the pedal and I mean all the way it will stay about 3000 rpm and will not go any higher if you barely take your foot off the throttle the engine dies.  Anyone who has any ideas I would greatly apreciate it.  Also does anyone know what it would take to put an pre 88 cradle complete with v6 engine and auto tranny into an 84 auto coupe.  Thanks Dennis||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-22-2001||02:49 AM||||1st post?  Welcome!<P>3000rpm at startup?  I think grinthock has(had) the same problem.  This thread is pretty recent, look back a couple of days.<P>Things to check:<BR>Vacuum Leaks<BR>EGR tube leak<BR>IAC<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000002||dennis_6||08-22-2001||02:57 AM||||Appreciate the info and greeting.  New to this BB not new to Fiero’s though.    ||||reg||1
Z||000003||heavyhorse||08-22-2001||12:15 PM||||Sounds similar to a problem I had on my 1986 V6.  It was the catalyic converter.  With the car cold, try opening the exhaust at the flange upstrea from the cat converter and see if it runs any better.<P>I'm new to Pennock's too!  It's great!||||reg||1
Z||000004||dennis_6||08-22-2001||05:09 PM||||I found my problem my car has a gas leak!  I had a two foot flame to prove it.  Flame was right around distributor.  I figure the spark from the rotor button making connections set the gas off.  Lucky I did have fireworks I guess.  Thanks to everyone who gave input.         Dennis||||reg||4
